# docs/static/openapi.yml is COMMITTED, deliberately.  app/app.go embeds it via docs/docs.go's
# `//go:embed static`, so its CONTENTS end up in the qadenad binary -- and a reproducible build must
# depend only on committed inputs.  While it was ignored, a clean checkout could not build at all
# (`pattern static: no matching files found`), and two machines that happened to hold different
# copies would have produced different binaries with nothing to point at why.
# Regenerate with `ignite generate openapi`; the output is deterministic (verified byte-identical
# across three machines).
cmd/qadenad_enclave/reproducible_build_signer_id.txt
cmd/qadenad_enclave/reproducible_build_unique_id.txt
cmd/qadenad_enclave/qadenad_enclave
# `go build ./cmd/qadenad_enclave/` writes the binary into the CURRENT directory, so a build run
# from the repo root leaves a 77MB artifact there.  It was committed three times before anyone
# noticed; ignored by absolute path so `git add -A` can never sweep it up again.
/qadenad_enclave
/qadenad
cmd/qadenad_enclave/qadenad_enclave.unsigned
cmd/qadenad_enclave/enclave_params.json
# The signer enclave's generated files, which were missed when it was added -- the qadenad_enclave
# equivalents above have been ignored all along.  Not cosmetic: an SGX build WRITES these, so
# leaving them tracked made the working tree permanently dirty on any SGX machine, and
# build_enclave.sh --build-sgx reacts to a dirty tree by running `git checkout -f && git clean -fd`.
# Every reproducible build therefore discarded whatever uncommitted work happened to be present,
# announcing it only as "WARNING!!! Untracked or modified files detected, removing them."
/docker_build_signer_enclave/output/
cmd/signer_enclave/reproducible_build_signer_id.txt
cmd/signer_enclave/reproducible_build_unique_id.txt
cmd/signer_enclave/signer_enclave
cmd/signer_enclave/signer_enclave.unsigned
cmd/qadenad/qadenad
*~
testkey
# Phase A token-gating: release artifacts and helper binary are fetched/built, not committed.
